msgid ""
"## <i class=\"fas fa-video\"></i> Watch Video\n"
"{{< youtube SJuScDavstM >}}"
msgstr ""
"## <i class=\"fas fa-video\"></i> 動画を観る\n"
"{{< youtube SJuScDavstM >}}"

#: physics/character_vs_rigid.md
msgid "### Infinite Inertia"
msgstr "### 無限の慣性力"

#: physics/character_vs_rigid.ja.md physics/character_vs_rigid.md
msgid "![alt](/godot_recipes/4.x/img/2d_physics_layers_01.png)"
msgstr "![alt](/godot_recipes/4.x/img/2d_physics_layers_01.png)"

#: physics/character_vs_rigid.ja.md physics/character_vs_rigid.md
msgid "![alt](/godot_recipes/4.x/img/char_push_inf.gif)"
msgstr "![alt](/godot_recipes/4.x/img/char_push_inf.gif)"

#: physics/character_vs_rigid.md
msgid ""
"Here, you can also see the downside of this option. Because the physics of "
"the boxes is being ignored, they can clip through walls and you can't jump "
"on top of them."
msgstr ""
"このオプションの欠点もここに現れています。箱の物理演算が無視されているため、"
"壁を貫通したり、上に乗ることすらできません。"

#: physics/character_vs_rigid.md
msgid ""
"Download the project's example code here: [https://github.com/godotrecipes/"
"character_vs_rigid](https://github.com/godotrecipes/character_vs_rigid)"
msgstr ""
"プロジェクトのサンプルコードはこちらからダウンロードできます：[https://"
"github.com/godotrecipes/character_vs_rigid](https://github.org/godotrecipes/"
"character_vs_rigid)"

#: physics/character_vs_rigid.md
msgid ""
"To give the colliding body a \"push\" we'll need to apply an impulse. An "
"impulse is an instantaneous \"kick\" - think of a bat hitting a ball. This "
"is as opposed to a force, which is a continuous \"push\" on an object."
msgstr ""
"衝突する物体に「押し」を与えるには、インパルスを適用する必要があります。イン"
"パルスとは瞬間的な「衝撃」のことで、野球でバットがボールを打つようなイメージ"
"です。これは、物体に対して連続的に力を加えるフォースとは異なります。"

#: physics/character_vs_rigid.ja.md physics/character_vs_rigid.md
msgid "![alt](/godot_recipes/4.x/img/physics_layers_box.png)"
msgstr "![alt](/godot_recipes/4.x/img/physics_layers_box.png)"

#: physics/character_vs_rigid.md
msgid ""
"By default, a {{< gd-icon CharacterBody2D >}}`CharacterBody2D` moved with "
"`move_and_slide()` or `move_and_collide()` will not push any {{< gd-icon "
"RigidBody2D >}}`RigidBody2D` it collides with. The rigid body doesn't react "
"at all, and behaves just like a {{< gd-icon StaticBody2D >}}`StaticBody2D`."
msgstr ""
"デフォルトでは、 `move_and_slide()` または `move_and_collide()` で移動させた "
"`CharacterBody2D` は、衝突する任意の `RigidBody2D` を押しません。リジッドボ"
"ディは全く反応せず、単なる `StaticBody2D` と同じように振る舞います。"

#: physics/character_vs_rigid.md
msgid ""
"The collision normal points *out* of the rigid body, so we reverse it to "
"point away from the character and apply the `push_force` factor. Now pushing "
"works again, but it won't force the rigid bodies through walls:"
msgstr ""
"衝突正規ベクトルは剛体の外側を指しているため、これを反転させてキャラクターか"
"ら離れる方向に調整し、`push_force` 係数を適用します。これで再び押す動作が可能"
"になりますが、壁越しに剛体を移動させることはできません。："

#: 2D/coyote_time.md 2D/moving_platforms.md physics/character_vs_rigid.md
msgid "- [Platform character](/godot_recipes/4.x/2d/platform_character/)"
msgstr ""
"- [プラットフォームキャラクタ](/godot_recipes/4.x/ja/2d/platform_character/)"

#: physics/character_vs_rigid.md
msgid ""
"For some games, this will be fine. If you want to prevent the clipping, "
"you'll need to go with option 2."
msgstr ""
"一部のゲームではこれで問題ありませんが、クリッピングを防ぎたい場合はオプショ"
"ン2を選択してください。"

#: physics/character_vs_rigid.md
msgid ""
"1. You can just push them, ignoring physics. If you're familiar with Godot "
"3.x, this is equivalent to the \"infinite inertia\" option.\n"
"1. You can give them a push based on the character's imagined \"mass\" and "
"velocity. This will give you a \"realistic\" result - pushing heavy bodies a "
"little, and lighter bodies a lot."
msgstr ""
"1. 物理学を無視して直接押すことも可能です。Godot 3.x に慣れている方なら、これ"
"は「無限慣性」オプションと同等の機能です。\n"
"1. キャラクターの想定する「質量」と「速度」に基づいて押力を発揮させることもで"
"きます。これにより「リアルな」結果が得られます - 重い物体は少し、軽い物体は大"
"きく押し出されるようになります。"

