#: 2D/autotile_intro.ja.md 2D/autotile_intro.md
msgid ""
"1. Switch back to the **Tiles** tab in the TileSet editor.\n"
"2. Select your tiles.\n"
"3. In the **Terrains** painting mode, click and drag over the tiles to "
"define which parts of the tile belong to which terrain. This replaces the "
"old \"Bitmask\" system."
msgstr ""

#: 2D/autotile_intro.ja.md 2D/autotile_intro.md
msgid ""
"- **Multiple Layers**: Godot 4 TileMaps support multiple layers natively, so "
"you can have terrains on different layers.\n"
"- **Multiple Terrains**: Different terrains can be set to interact with each "
"other in the same set.\n"
"- **Better UI**: The painting interface is much more intuitive than the "
"bitmask grid."
msgstr ""

#: 2D/autotile_intro.ja.md 2D/autotile_intro.md
msgid ""
"1. Select your `TileMap` node and go to the **TileSet** property.\n"
"2. In the **TileSet** editor at the bottom, go to the **Terrains** tab.\n"
"3. Add a **Terrain Set**. A \"Terrain Set\" is a group of terrains that can "
"interact with each other.\n"
"4. Set the **Mode** (usually \"Match Corners and Sides\" for most 16-tile or "
"48-tile sets).\n"
"5. Add a **Terrain** inside the set and give it a name and color."
msgstr ""

#: 2D/autotile_intro.ja.md
msgid "### セットアップ方法 Terrains"
msgstr ""

#: 2D/autotile_intro.ja.md 2D/autotile_intro.md
msgid ""
"> [!NOTE]\n"
"> **Godot 3 to 4 Migration**:\n"
"> - \"Autotile\" is now **Terrains**.\n"
"> - \"Bitmask\" is replaced by the Terrain painting mode in the TileSet "
"editor.\n"
"> - The logic is more flexible but requires a slightly different setup in "
"the TileSet resource."
msgstr ""

#: 2D/autotile_intro.ja.md 2D/autotile_intro.md
msgid ""
"1. Go to the `TileMap` editor in the main viewport area.\n"
"2. Select the **Terrains** tab.\n"
"3. Select your terrain and start painting! The engine will automatically "
"pick the matching tiles."
msgstr ""

#: 2D/autotile_intro.ja.md 2D/autotile_intro.md
msgid ""
"In Godot 4, the \"Autotile\" system from Godot 3 has been replaced by a much "
"more powerful **Terrains** system. Terrains allowed you to paint tiles and "
"have the engine automatically handle corners and edges."
